WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.880
Suppose you want a mouse in which one type of neuron glows when its calcium rises.

2
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.660
You also want to switch that same type on with light.

3
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.380
Put the gene for green fluorescent protein behind a promoter that every cell reads,

4
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.040
and you get a green mouse.

5
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:25.960
But you need the tools in one cell type, and nowhere else. How?

6
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:28.723
Two kinds of tool do the work.

7
00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:34.263
A reporter is an engineered protein that changes its light when a signal happens.

8
00:00:35.143 --> 00:00:39.143
GCaMP is a calcium reporter, built from green fluorescent protein.

9
00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:44.343
An actuator is an engineered protein that starts a signal on command.

10
00:00:45.463 --> 00:00:47.423
Channelrhodopsin-2 is an actuator.

11
00:00:48.183 --> 00:00:55.103
Blue light opens its pore, cations flow into the neuron, and at threshold the neuron fires.

12
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.007
Now give each gene a stop.

13
00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:04.527
Put a stop signal in front of the reporter gene, between two sites called loxP.

14
00:01:05.307 --> 00:01:07.567
The two sites point the same way.

15
00:01:08.287 --> 00:01:12.027
The actuator gene gets its own stop in the same way.

16
00:01:12.627 --> 00:01:15.467
With the stop in place, neither gene is read.

17
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:19.837
Cre is an enzyme from a bacterial virus.

18
00:01:20.457 --> 00:01:23.877
It cuts and rejoins DNA at loxP sites.

19
00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:29.697
When two sites point the same way, Cre removes what lies between them.

20
00:01:30.117 --> 00:01:31.477
The stop is cut out.

21
00:01:32.237 --> 00:01:36.057
Now the gene is read, in that cell and in all its descendants.

22
00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:43.570
So who makes Cre? Make it from a promoter that is active in one cell type.

23
00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.610
That cell type cuts out the stops, and makes both proteins.

24
00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.490
Every other cell makes no Cre.

25
00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.130
Its stops stay in place, and it makes neither protein.

26
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.580
To build the mouse, breed three parts together.

27
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.420
The first is Cre, placed in a gene that only your neuron type reads.

28
00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.860
The second is a reporter behind a stop.

29
00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.380
The third is an actuator behind a stop.

30
00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:17.640
Only cells that make Cre remove the stops, so only they make both proteins.

31
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:24.720
Keep this rule. Tools wait behind stops, and only cells that make Cre remove them.
